continuation:
The pencil in Bouchra’s hair spun; her grin widened. “Arr, calm yer keel, matey—ye’ll find these plates be as stout as a treasure chest under a kraken’s grip.”

Aurelio blinked once, decided the shed was not safe after all, and rolled with it. “Okay, so if I use them, what adhesive should I run on the bottom?”

“Shiver me timbers, epoxy be the way;

Ovid’s eyelids lowered; the postcard stopped dancing. “Prithee, good scholar, curb thy tempest. Thou seek’st counsel and dost find it wanting, yet wrath is but a jest unto experience.”

Noor blinked once, then barreled on. “Fine. If I crop, how tight without the lace fraying at the edge of frame?”

“Leave half the breadth of thy thumbnail betwixt the veil and the glass;

Silvio sighed, the sound rattling like a loose ceiling tile. “Honestly, I’m not the guy. Talk to Atiq; he’s the one who signed the last audit.”

Ranya felt the familiar heat rise behind her ears. “Atiq’s on leave. You’re the only one here with commit history on 6.2.”

“Commit history doesn’t mean I’m still awake. Look, I’m late already.” He edged past her;
